.TH IAD\-AUTOCOMPLETE 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
autocomplete \- an entry whose suggestions come from an asynchronous lookup (a database, an HTTP call), shown in a popover under it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
Autocomplete::new(value: &'a str, lookup: &'a Lookup<String, T>, on_input: impl Fn(String) \-> M + 'a)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBAutocomplete\fR: an entry whose suggestions come from an asynchronous lookup (a database, an HTTP call), shown in a popover under it.
.PP
A thin applier of \fBprimitives::lookup\fR: the app owns the text and the \fBLookup\fR state, and drives the async side with \fBcrate::lookup\fR. The widget draws what the lookup's status says and reports what the user does:
.PP
| Status | Popover | | \-\-\- | \-\-\- | | \fBIdle\fR | closed | | \fBWaiting\fR / \fBLoading\fR, no results yet | "Searching..." with a spinner | | \fBWaiting\fR / \fBLoading\fR, previous results | those results (the entry shows a spinner) | | \fBLoaded\fR | the suggestions, or "No results" | | \fBFailed\fR | the error and a Retry button (\fBon_retry\fR) |
.PP
.nf
.RS
Autocomplete::new(&self.text, &self.cities, Msg::Input)
    .label(|c: &City| c.name.clone())
    .on_select(Msg::Picked)
    .on_retry(Msg::Retry)
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBInteraction\fR
.PP
The popover opens when the user types or clicks the entry and there is something to show, and closes on a pick, Escape, or a click elsewhere. It is as wide as the entry and aligned to its start edge. Up / Down move the highlight (wrapping), Enter picks the highlighted suggestion, Escape closes. Hovering a row highlights it and a click picks it. Keys are read by the popover while it is open, so they work whatever the focus; Down reopens a closed popover only while the entry was last clicked in (the widget cannot ask the text input whether it has focus). Without a highlight Enter does nothing here (the text is yours).
.PP
After a pick, \fBon_select(item)\fR fires; set the text to the item's label yourself. The widget does not reopen the popover for that change.
.PP
\fBFree text\fR
.PP
\fBfree_text(true)\fR (the default) accepts any text. With \fBfalse\fR the text must be the label of a suggestion the user picked: keep the picked label in your state and pass it to \fBselected\fR; the entry then draws its error ring once \fBrevealed\fR, and \fBvalidity\fR / \fBlookup::validate_pick\fR give the same \fBValidity\fR for a \fBField\fR message or a form.
